Radio frequency gallium nitride (RF GaN) devices are semiconductor components designed for high-frequency and high-power applications. GaN's wide bandgap, high electron mobility, and thermal performance make it suitable for applications requiring power efficiency, signal amplification, and reliable operation at demanding frequencies.

RF GaN devices are used in wireless infrastructure, defense electronics, radar, satellite communications, and other radio-frequency systems. As communication networks and electronic systems require higher performance, manufacturers are investing in GaN-based transistors, power amplifiers, and integrated microwave circuits.

